## Criteria

*One line per checklist item for the gate, in the checklist's order. States: `pass` · `fail` ·
`waived` (only the user — the line is repeated in Waivers) · `exempt-by-profile` (only what the
checklist marks as waivable in the project's profile). A `fail` with no waiver = Result "failed".
"Tested" with no output is not evidence (`Maestro/core/quality-gates.md` §Anti-patterns).*

| Criterion (checklist section) | State (pass / fail / waived / exempt-by-profile) | Evidence (§Live proof format from Maestro/knowledge/proven-patterns.md: what · where · literal output · when · who) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| {{e.g. definition-of-done §F5 — state machines for the critical flows}} | {{pass}} | {{what: 3 state machines · where: `product/04-specification/state-machines.md` · literal output: "order: 6 states, 9 transitions, 0 guardless transitions" · when: yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm · who: architecture-reviewer}} |
| {{e.g. pre-merge §Tests — green suite on frontend and backend}} | {{pass}} | {{what: test command · where: apps/api, apps/web · literal output: "142 passed, 0 failed, exit 0" and "88 passed, exit 0" · when: yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm · who: harness in CI, run #…}} |
| {{e.g. definition-of-done §F4 — performance budgets per route}} | {{exempt-by-profile}} | {{marking *(waivable in: prototype)* in the checklist; project profile: prototype}} |

## Waivers

*Only the user waives; the agent never does (`Maestro/core/quality-gates.md` §Anatomy of a gate).
Empty = "none". A waiver is their decision, recorded with the why and the risk assumed — not a
shortcut.*

